This repository contains the reference implementation of MAGIC and the
code used to reproduce the results reported in the paper.

Baselines compared against in the paper (SCI, VCD, M3ID, TIE) are not
vendored here; only frozen result snapshots used for comparison are
included where noted in experiments/data/.

`pipeline/vlmeval/` is a trimmed copy of a private fork of VLMEvalKit v0.2
(https://github.com/open-compass/VLMEvalKit), Copyright VLMEvalKit
Authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Only the two backbone
model wrappers this project patched (`vlm/qwen2_vl/`, `vlm/llava/`) plus
the core framework they require are included; the ~60 other model
wrappers and the commercial-API adapters from the upstream fork are not.
The `qwen2_vl/model.py` and `llava/llava.py` files in this trimmed copy
contain modifications made for this project (VCF/TCF perturbation
handling, logit-dump hooks) on top of the upstream VLMEvalKit code; see
the top-level README's Scope section and `pipeline/README.md` for what
this pipeline does and does not reproduce.
